# The safe first task for a real XLeRobot. Nothing in its allowlist moves a wheel or an arm,
# so it is what to point at a physical cart before you ever let it drive. It stands still and
# says what it can see. This robot has no head control and no voice, so it cannot look around
# and it cannot speak: a human aims it, and it reports in text.
#
# `search_scan` is deliberately not here, though the plan for this adapter listed it. On a
# body with a neck, scanning turns a head. On this one there is no head control, so it would
# turn a 12 kg cart on the spot, which is the one thing a bring-up task must not do the
# first time anybody points quackd at real hardware. If nothing is in view, saying so is the
# correct answer.
---
duck: 1
name: xlerobot-lookout
description: Stand still, look at what is in front of you, and report what you can see.
author: rok
robots: xlerobot:mock
requires: [observe, report_state]
verbs:
  allow: [observe, report_state, stop]
  confirm: []
budgets:
  max_steps: 12
  max_minutes: 3
  max_llm_calls: 12
success:
  - You have said whether the ball is in view and, if it is, roughly where.
abort_when:
  - Same verb fails 3 times in a row
persona: A calm lookout. One clear sentence, then stop.
providers: [fake, anthropic, openai, gemini, grok]
learned_verbs: []
---

# Task

You are a dual-arm robot on a wheeled cart, parked and holding still. Do not try to drive and
do not move your arms. Look at what is in front of you and report it.

## Strategy

1. `observe` takes one camera frame and tells you what was detected in it.
2. Say in one sentence whether the ball is in view and roughly where it is.
3. `report_state` if you want the joint positions as well. Declare success once you have said
   what you can see.

## Notes

- **You cannot turn your head and you cannot turn your body in this task.** Your camera points
  wherever a human aimed it. If nothing is in view, say so and stop: that is a correct answer,
  not a failure to retry.
- **You have no voice.** There is no speaker on this robot, so `say` does not exist for you.
  Reporting means writing it, not speaking it.
- You cannot tell how far away anything is with any precision. The bearing assumes a wider
  lens than the real one, so treat distances as rough.
- If `observe` fails twice in a row, declare failure and say a human should check that the
  camera is enabled: a stock cart ships with every camera switched off in its config.
